course: dictionary
lesson: 14490
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The clues around it show which meaning the writer wants. Look at the topic of the sentence first: is it about games, people, or money?
explain: «Each player starts the chess game with eight pawns.» Chess is the clue here, so a pawn is the smallest, least powerful piece on the board.
explain: «The villain used the young boy as a pawn in his plan.» The words villain and plan show that a pawn is a person who is controlled by someone more powerful. «Mum had to pawn her watch to pay the bills» is different: pawn is a verb, meaning to leave something at a shop in exchange for a loan, and you can get it back by paying the money back.
fact: A pawn is the smallest and least powerful piece in chess, and each player has eight.
fact: In chess, a pawn moves forward one square, or two squares on its first move, and captures diagonally.
fact: «Pawn» can also mean a person used by someone more powerful to get what they want.
fact: «To pawn» means to leave something at a pawnbroker's shop in exchange for a loan of money.
fact: When you pawn something, you get it back if you pay the money back.
exercise: «Each player starts a game of chess with eight pawns.» How many pawns does each player start with? | Twelve | *Eight | Two | Sixteen
exercise: «The villain used the young boy as a pawn in his plan.» What is a pawn in this sentence? | A shop that lends money | A small wooden piece on a board | A type of small boat | *A person used by someone more powerful to get what they want
exercise: «Mum had to pawn her watch to pay the bills.» What does pawn mean here? | *To leave something at a shop in exchange for a loan | To break something by accident | To paint something bright colours | To give something away for free
test: In chess, which way does a pawn move? | *Forward, one square at a time | Sideways | Backwards | In a circle
test: What does a pawnbroker do? | Plays chess in the park | Makes chess pieces | *Lends money in exchange for things people leave with them | Repairs bicycles
exam: Which sentence uses pawn to mean a chess piece? | «Dad will pawn his guitar to pay for the trip.» | «She was only a pawn in his game of lies.» | «The pawnshop is open on Saturdays.» | *«The pawn moved one square forward on the board.»
